{{!
    @template mod_rememberme/report_coverage

    Per learner coverage and retention, plus the cohort review load forecast.

    Coverage is how much of the pool a learner has met at all; established is
    how much of it they hold at or above the instance's stability floor. The
    gap between the two columns is the interesting number: a learner who has
    seen everything and established little is cramming rather than retaining.

    The forecast is a plain count of items falling due on each of the coming
    days. It is drawn from the cached duedate column, which is written
    suspension aware, so a holiday shows up as a flat stretch rather than as a
    cliff on the day the holiday ends. Each bar carries its own count as text,
    so the chart is readable without seeing the bar.

    The learner value arrives already escaped with s() and is rendered
    unescaped on purpose. Every other value is escaped by the template engine.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasrows Boolean Whether there are any participants to list
    * pooltotal Number How many questions the pool holds
    * stabilityfloor String The stability in days at which an item counts as established
    * rows Array of rows, each with:
        * learner String The learner's full name, already escaped
        * seen Number Items the learner has memory state for
        * poolseen String That as a whole number percentage of the pool
        * established Number Items at or above the stability floor
        * poolestablished String That as a whole number percentage of the pool
        * meanstability String Mean stability in days across items seen
        * lapses Number Total lapses
        * started Boolean Whether the learner has answered anything
    * forecast Object with:
        * hasload Boolean Whether anything is due or overdue
        * overdue Number Items already overdue across the cohort
        * overduewidth Number Bar width for the overdue count, 0 to 100
        * days Array of days, each with label String, count Number, width Number

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasrows": true,
        "pooltotal": 180,
        "stabilityfloor": "14.00",
        "rows": [
            {
                "learner": "Aisha Karim",
                "seen": 140,
                "poolseen": "78",
                "established": 96,
                "poolestablished": "53",
                "meanstability": "21.40",
                "lapses": 18,
                "started": true
            },
            {
                "learner": "Tom Boyd",
                "seen": 0,
                "poolseen": "0",
                "established": 0,
                "poolestablished": "0",
                "meanstability": "0.00",
                "lapses": 0,
                "started": false
            }
        ],
        "forecast": {
            "hasload": true,
            "overdue": 12,
            "overduewidth": 40,
            "days": [
                {"label": "01 September", "count": 30, "width": 100},
                {"label": "02 September", "count": 9, "width": 30}
            ]
        }
    }
}}
<div class="mod_rememberme-report mod_rememberme-report-coverage">
    <p class="text-muted">
        {{#str}}poolsize, mod_rememberme, {{pooltotal}}{{/str}}
        {{#str}}establishedat, mod_rememberme, {{stabilityfloor}}{{/str}}
    </p>

    {{#hasrows}}
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-striped generaltable">
            <caption>{{#str}}reportcoveragecaption, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}learner, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}itemsseen, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}itemsestablished, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}meanstability, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    <th scope="col">{{#str}}lapses, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {{#rows}}
                <tr>
                    <th scope="row" class="font-weight-normal">{{{learner}}}</th>
                    <td>
                        {{#started}}{{seen}} ({{poolseen}}%){{/started}}
                        {{^started}}{{#str}}notstarted, mod_rememberme{{/str}}{{/started}}
                    </td>
                    <td>
                        {{#started}}{{established}} ({{poolestablished}}%){{/started}}
                        {{^started}}{{#str}}notstarted, mod_rememberme{{/str}}{{/started}}
                    </td>
                    <td>{{meanstability}}</td>
                    <td>{{lapses}}</td>
                </tr>
                {{/rows}}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    {{/hasrows}}
    {{^hasrows}}
        <p class="text-muted">{{#str}}reportnodata, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</p>
    {{/hasrows}}

    <h3 class="h5 mt-4">{{#str}}forecast, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</h3>
    <p class="text-muted">{{#str}}forecast_help, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</p>

    {{#forecast}}
        {{#hasload}}
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table generaltable mod_rememberme-forecast">
                <caption>{{#str}}forecastcaption, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">{{#str}}day, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                        <th scope="col">{{#str}}itemsdue, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                        <th scope="col">{{#str}}relativeload, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row" class="font-weight-normal">{{#str}}overduenow, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</th>
                        <td>{{overdue}}</td>
                        <td class="w-50">
                            <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true">
                                <div class="progress-bar bg-secondary" style="width: {{overduewidth}}%"></div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    {{#days}}
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row" class="font-weight-normal">{{label}}</th>
                        <td>{{count}}</td>
                        <td class="w-50">
                            <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true">
                                <div class="progress-bar" style="width: {{width}}%"></div>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    {{/days}}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        {{/hasload}}
        {{^hasload}}
            <p class="text-muted">{{#str}}reportnodata, mod_rememberme{{/str}}</p>
        {{/hasload}}
    {{/forecast}}
</div>
